Description: segment: drop reference_stream_first_pts end_pts adjustment
 Jellyfin-ffmpeg (and upstream FFmpeg 7.x) adds an automatic offset on
 segment muxer's `end_pts` equal to the first reference-stream
 packet's PTS. The intent: align segment split boundaries to an
 absolute-time axis so streams with non-zero start PTS (live capture,
 -copyts after -ss) still split at `segment_time` intervals counted
 from the FIRST packet rather than from PTS=0.
 .
 In practice, on Plex Windows segmented-mkv shape (`-f segment
 -segment_format matroska -segment_format_options live=1 -segment_time 1
 -copyts -ss N`), this adjustment defeats segment splitting entirely:
 with `-ss 162`, the first ref-stream packet has pts ≈ 162042000 µs,
 so `end_pts` for segment 0 becomes `1000000 + 162042000 = 163042000`
 µs. Empirically verified 2026-05-13 on jellyfin-ffmpeg 7.1.3 +
 scaleplex-ffmpeg7 with HEVC VAAPI and libx264 SW: 12 seconds of
 encoded video lands in chunk-00000 with zero splits, regardless of
 `-force_key_frames`.
 .
 Plex's own ffmpeg fork (FFmpeg 6.x base) has no equivalent
 adjustment — its `seg_write_packet` operates directly on raw
 `end_pts = seg->time * (segment_count + 1)`. Split fires on every
 keyframe past the first packet whose pts exceeds `end_pts -
 time_delta`. With Plex's force-keyframe expr (`gte(t, n_forced * 1)`)
 producing IDRs every second, that yields one chunk per second as
 designed.
 .
 This patch deletes the jellyfin first-pts adjustment in the
 scaleplex-ffmpeg fork, restoring upstream-pre-jellyfin behaviour
 which is what Plex's transcoder relies on. The downstream effect is
 that `chunk-NNNNN` files split at `segment_time` boundaries, and
 Cluster.Timecode in each chunk reflects source-time absolute PTS
 (with `-copyts` kept) without any relay-side post-patching.
 .
 Required follow-ups (separate commits):
   - worker rewriter: stop stripping `-copyts` on seek for matroska
     segment output and stop emitting `scaleplex_mkv_offset_ms` on
     `-segment_list` URLs.
   - shim relay: `patchSessionMatroskaChunks` becomes dead code on
     the matroska path; left in place as a defensive no-op until
     the rewriter side ships.
 .
 Reverting the adjustment in this fork is preferred over adding a
 new opt-in flag, because every scaleplex-driven session that
 reaches `-f segment -segment_format matroska` is a Plex Windows
 client expecting Plex-style split cadence. There is no scenario
 where the jellyfin behaviour is desirable for us.
Origin: drop, https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin-ffmpeg
Forwarded: not-needed
Author: scaleplex
Last-Update: 2026-05-13
---
--- a/libavformat/segment.c
+++ b/libavformat/segment.c
@@ -117,7 +117,6 @@ typedef struct SegmentContext {
     int64_t initial_offset;    ///< initial timestamps offset, expressed in microseconds
     char *reference_stream_specifier; ///< reference stream specifier
     int   reference_stream_index;
-    int64_t reference_stream_first_pts;    ///< initial timestamp, expressed in microseconds
     int   break_non_keyframes;
     int   write_empty;

@@ -747,8 +746,6 @@ static int seg_init(AVFormatContext *s)
            seg->reference_stream_index,
            av_get_media_type_string(s->streams[seg->reference_stream_index]->codecpar->codec_type));

-    seg->reference_stream_first_pts = AV_NOPTS_VALUE;
-
     seg->oformat = av_guess_format(seg->format, s->url, NULL);

     if (!seg->oformat)
@@ -901,18 +898,6 @@ calc_times:
             pkt->flags & AV_PKT_FLAG_KEY,
             pkt->stream_index == seg->reference_stream_index ? seg->frame_count : -1);

-    if (seg->reference_stream_first_pts == AV_NOPTS_VALUE &&
-        pkt->stream_index == seg->reference_stream_index &&
-        pkt->pts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE) {
-        seg->reference_stream_first_pts = av_rescale_q(pkt->pts, st->time_base, AV_TIME_BASE_Q);
-    }
-
-    if (seg->reference_stream_first_pts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE) {
-        end_pts += (INT64_MAX - end_pts >= seg->reference_stream_first_pts) ?
-                    seg->reference_stream_first_pts :
-                    INT64_MAX - end_pts;
-    }
-
     if (pkt->pts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE)
         pkt_pts_avtb = av_rescale_q(pkt->pts, st->time_base, AV_TIME_BASE_Q);

